React JS for Beginners : Master the Core Concepts Before Building Apps

Starting React can feel confusing because most tutorials jump directly into components, props, state, hooks, and other features without first explaining how everything fits together.

This video takes a different approach.

Before deep-diving into React development, we first build a clear mental model of the core React concepts and understand why they exist, how they work together, and when you actually need them.

In this video, you’ll understand:

• What React actually is and why it is used
• How React fits into modern frontend development
• Components and component-based architecture
• Props and how data flows between components
• State and why React needs it
• Events and user interactions
• Rendering and re-rendering
• Hooks and why they matter
• Component lifecycle and effects
• Context and shared state
• Client-side routing
• API integration and asynchronous data
• How these concepts connect in a real React application
• What you should understand before starting serious React development

The goal is simple:

Understand React first → Connect the concepts → Then start building.

By the end, you should have a clear mental model of React instead of memorizing individual React features.

This video is especially useful if you are:
• Completely new to React
• Coming from HTML/CSS/JavaScript
• Following React tutorials but still feeling confused
• Preparing to work on an existing React application
• Looking to understand React before going deeper into development

